  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Annual Boiler Service Liverpool. Your Questions Answered.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Straight answers to what Liverpool homeowners and landlords ask most before they book.</p>
      <div class="pf-faq" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.5rem;">
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an annual boiler service cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>A standard annual boiler service costs £120, fixed price. That covers the full HHIC check and the certificate emailed the same day. A combined service and CP12 costs £175 in one visit. A boiler repair diagnosis costs £95 with no call-out fee and no hidden extras. Checkatrade puts the Liverpool average at £103 in a £82 to £148 range, so £120 sits mid-market for a full HHIC service by our engineers.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">LEGAL</span>&nbsp; Is an annual boiler service a legal requirement?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>For homeowners, no. But the <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/domestic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">HSE</a>, <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safe Register</a> and all major makers strongly advise it. It is also a warranty condition. For landlords it is the law under the <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/landlords/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safety Regulations 1998</a>. Landlords must hold a valid CP12 and give a copy to tenants within 28 days.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">HOW OFTEN</span>&nbsp; How often should I service my boiler?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Every year. No exceptions. All major makers need a yearly service. This ensures your boiler keeps its warranty valid. Done by a Gas Safe engineer. Miss one year and a 10-year warranty can be void. A serviced boiler also runs up to 15% better, which means lower energy bills over the year. We put you on our annual reminder list after your first service.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">DIY</span>&nbsp; Can I service my own boiler?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>No. A gas boiler service must be done by a <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safe registered engineer</a>. It is the law under the Gas Safety Regulations. DIY gas work is illegal and dangerous. Always check your engineer's Gas Safe number before any gas work.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">FAULTS</span>&nbsp; What if a fault is found during the service?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>If we find a fault during the annual boiler service we explain what was found. We give you a written boiler repair quote first. We never start work without your explicit nod. You are never charged for work you have not agreed to. If a repair is needed, we can often do it on the same visit.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">TIME</span>&nbsp; How long does a boiler service take?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>A standard annual boiler service takes 45 minutes to 1 hour on most combi boilers. A combined service and gas safety certificate takes 60 to 75 minutes. We work fast and leave no mess.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">WARRANTY</span>&nbsp; Does an annual service protect my boiler warranty?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Yes. Worcester Bosch, Vaillant, Ideal and Baxi all need an annual service. Each one needs a Gas Safe engineer and an updated Benchmark certificate. Miss one year and a 10-year warranty can be void. That is a high quality boiler swapped years early at your cost. We follow the HHIC checklist and update Benchmark every visit.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">LANDLORDS</span>&nbsp; Do you provide the gas safety certificate landlords need?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Yes. Our combined annual boiler service and CP12 gas safety certificate costs £175 in one visit. Both documents are emailed the same day. The CP12 is accepted by all Liverpool letting agents, Liverpool City Council HMO licensing and the <a href="https://www.nrla.org.uk/resources/looking-after-your-property/landlords-gas-safety-responsibilities" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NRLA</a>. We work with landlords across all Liverpool postcodes and can coordinate tenant access.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:0.5rem;padding:0;"><summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:1rem 1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:#1a3a5c;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;"><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are you Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body" style="padding:0 1.25rem 1.25rem;border-top:1px solid #f1f5f9;"><p>Yes. Liverpool Emergency Plumber is Gas Safe registered. Verify at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. Every service is by our own employed Gas Safe engineers. All gas work is carried out by Gas Safe registered engineers.</p></div></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

